\begin{align*}
\tan V &= \frac{h}{XW} \\
&= \frac{h}{3}
\end{align*}

Now, we can use the Pythagorean theorem to find $h$:
\begin{align*}
h^2 + VW^2 &= VX^2 \\
h^2 + 3^2 &= (\sqrt{13})^2 \\
h^2 + 9 &= 13 \\
h^2 &= 4 \\
h &= 2
\end{align*}

Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\tan V &= \frac{h}{XW} \\
&= \frac{2}{3}
\end{align*}

